Modifications from upstream: the code was ported from CommonJS
JavaScript to TypeScript ES modules, and the rule-context APIs removed
in ESLint 9/10 were adapted (`context.getSourceCode()` ->
`context.sourceCode`, `context.getFilename()` -> `context.filename`,
`context.getScope()` fallbacks dropped in favor of
`context.sourceCode.getScope(node)`). Upstream's legacy
`environments.react-native` globals were not ported (no consumer used
them). Behavior is otherwise intended to be identical, and the unit
tests exercise every vendored rule on ESLint 10.
